node_modules

# The mock fixtures under tools/evaluation/mocks/ are self-contained projects
# with their own formatter (see e.g. tools/evaluation/mocks/tsuzuri/package.json)
# and their own conventions — reformatting them to this repository's house
# style would diverge them from what their own toolchain expects, so this
# repository's gates never cover them; the mock's own toolchain is what keeps
# it honest.
tools/evaluation/mocks/

# An evaluation's derived layer is regenerated and then compared BYTE FOR BYTE
# against what is committed, which is how a hand-edited summary is caught (the
# old effect evaluation's summarize.mjs --check did this). Those bytes come from exactly one
# serializer — layout.mjs's `canonicalJson` — so a second formatter with an
# opinion about them would make the drift check fail against a file the
# instrument never wrote. The measured files under measurements/ are excluded
# for the plainer reason that nothing here authored them.
#
# Deliberately NOT the whole of tools/evaluation/data/: README.md and
# fixture.json are ordinary hand-written files and stay covered.
tools/evaluation/data/*/measurements/
tools/evaluation/data/*/summary.json
